.TH DU 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
du \- estimate file space usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B du
[\fB\-h\fR] [\fB\-s\fR] [\fIPATH\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Summarize disk usage of each PATH (the current directory by default) by summing file sizes recursively.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-human\-readable
Print sizes in human-readable form.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-summarize
Print only a total for each argument, not every subdirectory.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH NOTES
Hard-linked files are not deduplicated, unlike GNU du.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an I/O error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
